      'Since all labels are incorrect, the box labeled "Apples & Oranges" cannot have both fruits; it must be either all apples or all oranges. If you draw an apple from it, that box is definitely "Apples". The box labeled "Oranges" cannot be oranges (wrong label) and cannot be apples (already found), so it must be "Apples & Oranges". The box labeled "Apples" must therefore be "Oranges". Picking from "Apples & Oranges" guarantees complete deduction in 1 pick.',
