      'In a certain code language and logic game, four cards lie on a table. Each card has a letter on one side and a single-digit integer on the other. The visible faces are: [E], [K], [4], [7]. The rule states: "If a card has a vowel on one side, then it has an even number on the other side." Which cards MUST you turn over to test whether this rule is violated?',
