      'Initially, the probability that the car is behind Door 1 is 1/3, and the probability that it is behind Doors 2 or 3 combined is 2/3. Since Monty always reveals a goat from the unchosen doors, all 2/3 probability of the unchosen set collapses onto Door 2. Therefore, switching doubles your chance of winning from 1/3 to 2/3.',
