      'To transport bananas most efficiently, create intermediate drop depots: When carrying between 2000 and 3000 bananas, 5 trips are needed per km (3 forward, 2 return), consuming 5 bananas/km. Stop when stock drops to 2000: (3000 - 2000)/5 = 200 km. Stock at 200 km is 2000 bananas. Between 1000 and 2000 bananas, 3 trips per km are needed (2 forward, 1 return), consuming 3 bananas/km. Stop when stock drops to 1000: (2000 - 1000)/3 = 333.33 km. Travel 333 km to km 533, consuming 333*3 = 999 bananas, leaving 1001 bananas (or 1000 bananas at km 533.33). From km 533.33, camel carries 1000 bananas on a single trip to the end (distance 1000 - 533.33 = 466.67 km). Camel eats 467 bananas, delivering 1000 - 467 = 533 bananas.',
